# Environment — never commit real secrets, only .env.example
#
# Everything is matched and the example is added back, rather than listing the
# names in use: the previous list enumerated `.env.local`, `.env.production` and
# four others, so a file named anything else — `.env.prod`, say — was tracked by
# default. An ignore rule for secrets has to fail closed.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

